// The digit-sum forms of Legendre's formula and Kummer's theorem that used to
// live here are now proved in the number_theory package:
//
//   legendre_digit_sum(p, n)   —  p.is_prime implies
//       p * count_prime_factor(p, n.factorial) + digit_sum(p, n) =
//           n + count_prime_factor(p, n.factorial)
//   kummer_digit_sum(p, a, b)  —  p.is_prime implies
//       p * count_prime_factor(p, (a + b).binom(a)) + digit_sum(p, a + b) =
//           count_prime_factor(p, (a + b).binom(a)) +
//               digit_sum(p, a) + digit_sum(p, b)
//
// Both live in `src/number_theory/kummer.ac` (exported through the
// `number_theory` interface): `legendre_digit_sum` is proved by strong
// induction on the recursion budget of `digit_sum` using the merged
// `legendre_factorial_recurrence` and `digit_sum_recurrence`; `kummer_digit_sum`
// follows from `legendre_digit_sum` at `a`, `b`, `a+b` together with
// `kummer_digit_sum_of_legendre_digit_sum` and the merged `legendre_binom`.
// The carry-count form (`v_p(binom(a+b,a)) = addition_carry_count(p, a, b)`)
// is in `src/number_theory/kummer_carry.ac`.
